        "# QMarkdown playground\n\nEdit the source to see native Qt Quick rendering immediately. Try **strong**, *emphasis*, and `inline code`.\n\n## Wrapping and styling\nUse the width selector and style controls to explore wrapping. Each pane scrolls independently.\n\n``` cpp\n// Literal fenced code\nQString greeting = \"Hello, 日本語 😀\";\n```\n\n### Supported today\nParagraphs, H1–H6, inline formatting, escapes/entities, code blocks, Setext headings, thematic breaks, lists and quotes.\n\nLinks [example](https://example.invalid) report destinations to the host; images ![example](image.png) expose descriptions; <b>HTML</b> remains literal.",
